{"version":2,"text":"15. In the first paragraph, the writer mentions the role of 20th century\nliterature in\n\n(A) informing patients of the side effects of antipsychotic\nmedication.\n(B) preventing the mistreatment of defenceless people.\n(C) increasing the number of patients receiving ECT.\n\n(D) promoting a negative image of ECT.\n\n16. What do we learn about schizophrenia in the second paragraph?\n\n(A) It was less prevalent in patients who experienced seizures.\n(B) It had a significant impact on the treatment of epilepsy.\n(C) Many asylums in the UK were not prepared to treat it.\n(D) The medication metrazol could be used to induce it.\n\n17. What did the US National Institute of Mental Health decide in the 20th\ncentury?\n(A) Practitioners must follow identical treatment plans when using\n\nECT.\n\n(B) Patients should be given the right to refuse ECT treatment.\n(C) ECT should only be used as a treatment in severe cases.\n(D) ECT was accepted as a safe treatment for patients.\n\n18. In the fourth paragraph, what idea does the writer emphasise with the\n\nphrase ‘it goes without saying’?\n\n(A) Some women find ECT treatments successful while carrying a\nchild.\n(B) It is well known that some patients will not respond well to\nECT.\n\n(C) Few patients realise that they could benefit from ECT therapy.\n(D) The risks associated with ECT are rarely discussed.\n\nPage 79","layout":{"version":1,"width":612.0,"height":792.0,"blocks":[{"text":"15. In the first paragraph, the writer mentions the role of 20th century\nliterature in","lines":[{"text":"15. In the first paragraph, the writer mentions the role of 20th century","x":0.17792279901960784,"y":0.051281407828282825,"width":0.6615258071895423,"height":0.016527272727272734,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"15.","x":0.17792279901960784,"width":0.029411764705882353,"confidence":1},{"text":"In","x":0.22027574019607843,"width":0.019595606209150337,"confidence":1},{"text":"the","x":0.24575368137254902,"width":0.02873751